## New Qed proof: F continuity in nulhomotopy_R2_from_unbounded_component

### F continuity (translation homotopy avoids zero, F continuous to R2m0)

Proved the F continuity admit inside claim Hg_hom_k of
nulhomotopy_R2_from_unbounded_component.

The goal:
  continuous_map (setprod A unit_interval)
    (product_topology A TA unit_interval unit_interval_topology)
    R2m0 TR2m0
    (graph (setprod A unit_interval) (fun q => r2sub (g(q 0)) (alpha(q 1))))

Strategy:
1. Expand g: A -> R2m0 to g: A -> R2 (via subspace inclusion + congr_on)
2. Expand alpha: I -> R2 \ image(g,A) to alpha: I -> R2 (similar)
3. Build pi1: AI -> A, pi2: AI -> I (projections)
4. g_ext := g o pi1, alpha_ext := alpha o pi2 (both continuous AI -> R2)
5. h_pair := pair_map AI g_ext alpha_ext (continuous AI -> R2 x R2)
6. r2sub_map (continuous R2 x R2 -> R2) from R2_sub_map_continuous_early
7. h_comp := r2sub_map o h_pair (continuous AI -> R2)
8. Show h_comp agrees pointwise with F (using apply_fun_graph + claim+exact pattern)
9. F continuous to R2 via continuous_map_congr_on
10. F range in R2m0 via R2_translation_homotopy_avoids_zero_early
11. Conclude via continuous_map_range_restrict

